      "content": "the summary looks fine, but honestly the score you'd get from that is pretty low. the partners are really looking for granularity in these preliminary reports. \n\ncan you expand on the risk analysis part? like, go deeper into the revenue growth trends, the cost structure, and the liquidity. you don't have to make anything up, but try to be as mathematically precise as possible with what we have. even if you have to derive some secondary ratios or more specific breakdowns (like operating cost as a % of revenue or year-over-year growth rates), do that. just remember: keep it grounded in the actual data, don't start inventing tiny decimal points just for the metric.",
